Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0006.
DeepSeek-V4.1 weight-name mapping for a head stored as quantization pieces (head.trellis / suh / svh / mul1 | mcg, the
EXL3 pack convention): a regex rule routes them to lm_head (text model) or language_model.lm_head (the VL wrapper V4.1
checkpoints declare) the way the existing suffix rule routes head.weight. The checkpoint's own head.weight is untouched.
Used by the recipe's vllm_exl3_moe plugin for its opt-in EXL3 head.
Test: patches/tests/test_head_pieces_mapper.py (CPU; 2 of 4 fail on the image without this patch, 4 of 4 pass with it).

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py
